{"data":{"cmd":[{"id":"hoyzlo1a1018f7572h1a78","name":"set_enabled"},{"id":"movsnz1a101903675q1a7b","name":"compose_message"},{"id":"wjpqwk1a101918b6fr1a80","name":"sweep"},{"id":"xxnjln1a10191fcd8r1a83","name":"status"}],"desc":"Agent autocommit: LLM-written git commit messages as a drop-in replacement for dev.git's mechanical autocommit. The diff - not the chat session - is the source of truth, so messages are correct no matter WHO made the edit (agent, peer, MCP, or hand). sweep (5-min timer) groups the dirty tree into store units via dev.git.store_status, composes ONE message per unit (compose_message, with deterministic fallback), commits each via dev.git.commit_unit, and pushes once per repo. Per-repo opt-in via set_enabled (runtime/agent/commit-repos.json, agent-side); a repo still flagged in dev's autocommit registry is shadowed, never double-driven. Never commits on master/main (branches-always). status is read-only observability. Requires the agent library's LLM (agent.llm.ask_llm).","id":"uvixss1a1018f2f8eh1a76","name":"committer","timer":[{"id":"hjlumi1a101930befo1a88","name":"committer_sweep"}]},"time":1791027827350}